Item 01 is complete and the gate passes. Recap:

**The replay succeeded, after one relaunch.** The coordinator's run of 01:03 had already died when this session began: `lake build … -j 8` fails on Lake 5.0.0 (Lean v4.34.1 has no jobs option), so nothing of the family was compiled. I dropped the option, moved the eight-core cap to `taskset -c 0-7` on the `bwrap` line, fixed the Mathlib-rev log line, and relaunched once at 01:16 through a wrapper that keeps a live parent for `--die-with-parent`.

**Result of run 2** (`paper3/replay/logs/run2/`, regenerate with `bash paper3/replay/counts.sh`):

| quantity | value |
|---|---|
| exit code | 0, build 01:16:25 to 01:49:31 (33 min on 8 cores) |
| modules compiled | 3,091 distinct, identical to the audit's closure list |
| `error` / `sorry` lines | 0 / 0 |
| `#print axioms exact_count_and_sat` | `[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]` |
| versions | Lean 4.34.1 (5045d005), Lake 5.0.0, Mathlib d13f23b7 upstream |

The build log also records 19 in-source `#print axioms` outputs, all three standard axioms. The replay copy and the pristine clone are both at `4eaee875` with identical file hashes.

**The second kernel ran and passed.** `lean4export` v4.34.0 (built with the pinned 4.34.1) exported the theorem and its dependencies (2.36 GB NDJSON) in 68 s, and `nanoda_lib` 0.4.31 reported `Checked 95176 declarations with no errors` in 110 s with the three axioms permitted. The export holds exactly three axiom declarations. Item 12's nanoda reserve is not needed.

**Written:** `paper3/replay/README.md` (both scripts verbatim in both versions, timeline, counts, hashes, nanoda scripts recorded before they ran), `paper3/latex/sec5_replay.tex` ("Independent replay", ends with "what this does not claim"; `make check` passes, 6 pages), the `paper3/README.md` replay paragraph, entries 01a–01d in `ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD`, the PROGRESS.md section, and the item marked `[x]`. Gate: PASS. Nothing under `solutions/` touched; nothing committed, per the instructions.

**One thing to know:** `paper3/scripts/rho_over_n.py` and its figure and CSV appeared at 02:07 from another Claude session on this machine. They are not this item's work. The driver's `git add -A` will sweep them into this commit, and PROGRESS.md says so for item 02.

